---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
/* Template only, not legal advice. Have it reviewed before launch, especially if you add GA4, ads or an email list. */
const updated = 'November 5, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${site.name} handles your information.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <p class="lead">We built {site.name} to need as little information as possible. Here’s exactly what happens.</p>

      <h2>The gear guide</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you enter in the gear guide (your player’s name, age, measurements and other answers) is processed <strong>in your browser</strong> and saved
        <strong>only on your device</strong> (in your browser’s local storage) so you can come back to your plan. We never receive it. You can erase it at any time with the
        “Start over” button or by clearing your browser data.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you use “Share with family,” the link includes your answers (age, sizes and so on) so the recipient can see the same plan. It does <strong>not</strong> include
        your player’s name.
      </p>

      <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is written for parents and guardians, not for children. We don’t knowingly collect personal information from children, and the gear guide doesn’t send
        any information to us.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We may use privacy-friendly analytics to understand which pages are helpful (for example, page views and which guide steps people complete). This doesn’t include
        your gear guide answers or anything that identifies you. [Update this section to name your analytics provider before launch.]
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links and retailer cookies</h2>
      <p>
        When you click a shopping link, you go to the retailer’s site. The retailer or affiliate network may set cookies to record that you came from us, so we can be paid a
        commission. Their privacy policies apply on their sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Email (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        If you sign up for reminders, your email address is stored by our email provider and used only to send what you asked for. Every email has an unsubscribe link.
        [Name your email provider here before launch.]
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
